Description: Synthetic difference-in-differences, synthetic control and
    difference-in-differences estimates of the average treatment effect on
    the treated in panel data, following Arkhangelsky, Athey, Hirshberg,
    Imbens and Wager (2021) <doi:10.1257/aer.20190159> and the Stata
    implementation of Clarke, Pailanir, Athey and Imbens (2024)
    <doi:10.1177/1536867X241297914>. Supports simultaneous and staggered
    treatment adoption, bootstrap, jackknife and placebo inference,
    covariate adjustment, and parallel replications in compiled code.
    Derived from the synthdid package by the authors of the 2021 paper.
